<div class="marketing-page" data-controller="scroll-reveal">
<%= render 'shared/marketing_header' %>

<section class="mkt-hero" style="padding: 4rem 0 5rem;">
  <div class="mkt-inner">
    <span class="mkt-hero__eyebrow" style="margin-bottom: 1.25rem; display: inline-flex;">
      <span class="mkt-hero__eyebrow-dot"></span>
      Last updated: <%= Date.current.strftime("%B %d, %Y") %>
    </span>
    <h1 class="mkt-hero__title" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.5vw, 3.25rem);">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="mkt-hero__subtitle" style="max-width: 36rem;">
      Plain language for a small personal project. I have tried to keep this short.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="mkt-section bg-white">
  <div class="mkt-inner--narrow">

    <div class="mkt-highlight-box mkt-highlight-box--blue mkt-reveal" data-scroll-reveal-target="item" style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
      By using peponi.to you agree to these terms and the privacy policy.
      If you disagree, don’t use the hosted site — clone the repo instead.
    </div>

    <div class="mkt-prose mkt-reveal" data-scroll-reveal-target="item">

      <h2>What this is</h2>
      <p>
        Peponi.to is a day planner I built for myself. The code is MIT-licensed on
        <a href="<%= github_source_url %>">GitHub</a>. The website at peponi.to is a hosted sandbox:
        you can try the full app for seven days. After that I delete the account and the tasks on my server.
      </p>
      <p>
        There is no payment, no subscription, and no paid licence. If you want to keep your lists,
        run the app from source (self-host for sync, or one machine for local-only).
        The Omarchy plugin can stay local with no account at all.
      </p>

      <h2>Your content</h2>
      <p>
        Your lists belong to you. I don’t claim them. Export them before the hosted week ends
        if you want a copy. After deletion I cannot restore them.
      </p>

      <h2>The hosted week</h2>
      <p>
        On peponi.to I will send a reminder before I delete the account, when email is working.
        A PWA installed from peponi.to is still talking to my server. It will stop working when the week ends.
        Add to Home Screen against <em>your</em> instance if you want it on a machine you control.
      </p>

      <h2>Availability</h2>
      <p>
        I run a small droplet. I don’t promise uptime. I may change or stop the hosted site.
        The source stays yours to run.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        Don’t abuse the hosted site (spam accounts, attacks, illegal content). I may delete accounts that do.
      </p>

      <h2>Warranty</h2>
      <p>
        The software is provided “as is”, as the MIT licence says. I am not liable for lost lists
        or anything you do with a clone.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions: the <%= link_to "contact form", contact_path %>.
      </p>

    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<%= render 'shared/footer' %>
</div>
